    description: "scripts/release-check carries two --ignore-vuln flags added 2026-06-10 to unblock prepare-release 6.0.0, both for advisories with NO released fix at the time (verified fix_versions: [] via pip-audit -f json): (1) PYSEC-2026-139 — torch 2.10.0, transitive dep of the optional sentence-transformers embeddings extra; this one matters most because end users who install the embeddings extra get torch too. (2) CVE-2025-69872 — diskcache 5.6.3, pulled in only by llama_cpp_python (local LM experimentation, not a hypergumbo dependency in any extra). ACTION at each release prep (or when this surfaces in tracker ready): run pip-audit -f json (or check the advisories directly), and for each of the two: if a fixed version now exists, upgrade the local package, remove the corresponding --ignore-vuln flag + its comment block from scripts/release-check, and verify release-check passes. Close this item only when BOTH ignores are removed. Context thread: the 6.0.0 release-prep session 2026-06-10; the gate edit merged as 0b24486ac9."  # c4b8
